CloudBurrow patch 41 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1460). Applies after patch 0036.

The gap: BigQuery's FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF reads a table as it was at a
time in its time travel window
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/time-travel). Patch 0036's change
table records each row inserted, deleted and updated with the time of
its transaction, but a reader cannot tell which change is of which row,
nor the order of one transaction's changes, nor from when the change
table holds the whole history (an ALTER TABLE that rebuilds the table,
and CREATE OR REPLACE TABLE, start it over).

The patch gives every change table three pseudo-columns, which SELECT *
leaves out: googlesqlite_change_micros (the change time in microseconds),
googlesqlite_change_rowid (the changed row's rowid in the table) and
rowid (the change table's own rowid, the order of the changes); and
records, as the change table is made, a row of _CHANGE_TYPE 'START' at
the time it was made. The table as it was at a time is then, of each
rowid, the last change at or before that time, when it is not a DELETE.
CloudBurrow's front reads FOR SYSTEM_TIME AS OF so, and leaves the START
row out of APPENDS and CHANGES. change_history_rows_test.go fails
without the patch and passes with it; change_history_test.go (patch
0036) leaves the START row out of its reads.

